==English==
{{was wotd|2023|March|27}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|h₁epi}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}
The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|bestowen}}, {{m|enm|bistouen}}, {{m|enm|bistowen|t=to give, bestow; to apply (something to something else); to arrange or have control over (something); to place (someone) in a position; to use (for some purpose); (''reflexive'') to find (oneself) a place to live or shelter}}{{nb...|bestow, bestowe, bistow, bistowe, bystow, bystowe|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=bistouen|pos=v|id=MED4899}}</ref> from {{m|enm|bi-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} forming {{glossary|verb}}s, often with a completive, figurative, or intensive meaning}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=bi-|pos=''pref.''(2)|noformat=1|id=MED4326}}</ref> + {{m|enm|stouen}}, {{m|enm|stowen|t=to pack (cargo) in a ship, stow; to place (someone) in a certain position; to provide quarters for, lodge; etc.}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=stouen|pos=v|id=MED43137}}</ref><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=18218|date=March 2023}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|pos=v|source=Random House}}</ref> (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-|t=to place; to stand (up)}}). The English word is analysable as {{prefix|en|be|pos1={{glossary|intensifying}} prefix forming verbs|stow|t2=to put (something) away in a suitable place; etc.}}.

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the verb.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=18217|date=March 2023}}</ref>

